WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.205
These two chain ladders were dropped at exactly&nbsp;
the same time,

00:00:03.205 --> 00:00:05.344
by Cornell Professor Andy Ruina.

00:00:05.344 --> 00:00:07.663
The one on the right remains in free-fall,

00:00:07.663 --> 00:00:10.451
but the one on the left will hit a table.

00:00:10.451 --> 00:00:12.523
So which one will fall faster:

00:00:12.523 --> 00:00:13.876
The free falling ladder?

00:00:13.876 --> 00:00:15.468
The one that hits the table?

00:00:15.468 --> 00:00:17.520
Or will they both fall at the same rate?

00:00:24.181 --> 00:00:26.059
Now, why did that happen?

